    {
        "id": "f9d60f4c68faa702",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "Batch outbox",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Barebones batch delivery demo.\n\nBatch mode: a single claim emits msg.payload as an array of job payloads and msg.outbox.batch preserves the matching lease metadata. One PostgreSQL unnest statement processes them all, and batch-aware settlement partitions results into delivered, retrying, dead, and stale."
    },
    {
        "id": "demo-flow",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "Durable PostgreSQL outbox demo",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Generated readings are committed to SQLite before a worker attempts PostgreSQL delivery.\n\nWalk through the groups from left to right:\n1. Data Generation — create a sensor reading every 2s\n2. Queue — persist to the local SQLite outbox first\n3. Insert — poll the queue and deliver to PostgreSQL\n4. Retry — handle failures with classification and retry\n5. Operations — inspect, pause, resume, and recover\n6. Housekeeping — purge old deliveries (optional)"
    },
